      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{9}{5}x+32\\\\x&=\\frac{9}{5}y+32\\\\x-32&=\\frac{9}{5}y\\\\y&=\\frac{5}{9}(x-32)\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{5}{9}(x-32)\\end{align*}$$\nThe inverse takes a temperature $x$ in °F and returns its temperature in °C.",
